Since everyone has been talking about wishing, I decided to check out a  
theory, and so far it works!

The following theory is a major spoiler:
























Ok, this theory isn't 100% tried and true, so don't count on it.  But,  
here it is.

I played in wizard mode and wished for a wand of wishing with 3 charges.
Then, I used the wand of wishing to wish for 2 wand of wishings and a  
blessed scroll of charging. 
Then I noticed that both of the wand's of wishing that I created had  
charges, the first had 2 charges and the second had 1.
So, I used 2 charges for 2 more blessed scrolls of charging and 1 charge  
for a wand of wishing.  (The new wand had 1 charge.)
Then I used the scrolls of charging to charge the wands that I had gotten  
by using the inital wand of wishing to 3 charges.
Bingo, instead of 1 wand of wishing with 3 charges, I now have 3!
I carried this out one more time and had 27 total charges.  (don't charge  
a wand more than once as it may destroy the wand.)
After a while, one or two of the charges on newly charged wands would not  
work, but you still get way more wishes than you were given.
Also, I never saw a wand totally not work (ie. always one charge would  
work out of the three from the blessed charging scrolls.)

Realize, I was not using the control-w command, I was using the wands!

This seems to indicate that if you find a wand of wishing, wish for a wand  
of wishing and a blessed scroll of charging.
Then recharge the new wand (chances are it may have a few uses first.) and  
you can also have a fully charged wand on hand and still wish for the  
moon.

I have yet to try this out without wizard mode, I will today.

If someone finds a fault with this theory, tell me.


